WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.735
-The governor of Texas
threatened

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.137
to arrest Democratic lawmakers
who fled the state

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:07.907
to block a Draconian new
voter suppression law designed

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.575
to keep Republicans in power.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.911
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:15.949
♪♪

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.450
I'm sure I don't have
to remind you

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.719
that the 2020 election results
were, for the most part,

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:22.088
very bad for Republicans.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.557
Yes, they won back seats
in the House,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.393
but they lost the popular vote
by seven million to a Democrat

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.162
who got the most votes
in American history;

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.731
they lost the Electoral College
in a landslide;

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.099
and they even lost
several states

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.135
that were historically red,
like Georgia and Arizona,

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.403
where they also lost
all four Senate seats.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.637
In fact, Biden,

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:41.374
his win in Georgia
was confirmed so many times,

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.977
he turned it into a joke
when he was campaigning there

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.578
for the Democratic
Senate candidates.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.914
-Thank you for standing strong

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.249
to make sure
your voices were heard,

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.151
your votes were counted

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:53.386
and counted

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.621
and counted again!

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.022
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.958
I'm starting to feel like
I won Georgia three times.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.828
[ Horns blaring ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.196
-One of the few things I'll miss
about COVID-era politics

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:05.498
is the drive-in rallies.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.565
It's the only time in history

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:07.967
we'll be able to look back
and ask,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:11.204
"Was he giving a speech
or crossing against the light?"

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.006
I know it was Georgia,
but the sound of honking

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.306
just makes it feel
like New York,

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:15.308
like he should've been up there

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.109
with the Times Square Spider-Man

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.945
and a cigarette-smoking
cockroach.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.214
[ Smoker's voice ]
Can you believe
this Mets bullpen?

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.983
They blew a five-run lead
against the Pirates!

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.284
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.284 --> 00:01:26.819
What do you mean, I can't vote
because I'm a cockroach?

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.054 line:0%
I have a valid ID.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.556 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:33.025
It was like that stage is
in the middle of 42nd Street

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.460
during rush hour traffic.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.395
[ As Biden ]
I won Georgia three times.

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:39.165
[ New York accent ]
I don't care if you won
Miss America!

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.500
I got to get
this ass[bleep] to JFK!

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.403
[ Laughter ]
I'm sorry, did you just
call me an ass[bleep]?

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:44.604
[ New York accent ]
Oh, sorry, pal.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.873
I thought you couldn't hear me
over the Taxi TV.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.140
Actually, I'm trying
to turn down

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.909
the Taxi TV.
Do you know how to do that?

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.010
[ New York accent ]
Hey, I didn't put it there!

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.745
Take it up with Cat Greenleaf.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:56.215
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:58.284
Now, the losses in Georgia
and Arizona

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.552
really freaked out Republicans

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.687
because it meant
the electoral map was shifting.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:04.524
States that were traditionally
red were suddenly in play

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.559
and the GOP's built-in advantage

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.227
in the Electoral College
was eroding.

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.130
And that was especially
evident in Texas,

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.332
where Trump won
with the smallest margin

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.833
for a Republican in 24 years

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.869
and Biden got
the largest percentage

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.136
of any Democratic candidate

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.505
since Jimmy Carter
won the state in 1976.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.273
A fact that surprised me

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:22.709
because everything's bigger
in Texas,

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:25.611
but, according to this photo,
Jimmy Carter is super small.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.613
[ Laughter ]
When I was young and I heard him

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:31.050
referred to as a peanut farmer,
I assumed he farmed peanuts.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.020
But was he a farmer
the size of a peanut?

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.188
[ Laughter ]
Don't get me wrong.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.256
He's the best.
I love him.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.689
He's a world-renowned
humanitarian,

00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:38.791
human rights activist.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.726
I'm just saying,
judging from this photo,

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.461
if he tried to wear
a cowboy hat,

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:43.596
he'd get lost in it.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.697
[ As Carter ]
Rosalynn.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.499
Rosalynn, help.
I'm stuck in the hat.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:49.401
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:51.070
Again, as a reminder,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.039
I spent the last two weeks
in impression camp.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.640
[ Laughter ]
The point is,

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.308 line:0%
Republicans are terrified
of the possibility

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.745 line:0%
that Democrats could continue
making gains in Texas

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:01.080 line:0%
and potentially win
the state's electoral votes

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.581
in a future
presidential election.

00:03:02.581 --> 00:03:04.917
They're not hiding it
or being shy about it.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.019
Here's Texas
Lieutenant Governor Dan Patrick

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:08.921
at the Conservative
Political Action Conference

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:11.123
over the weekend,
telling the crowd

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:14.393
that, if they lose Texas,
they'll lose the entire country.

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:18.330 line:0%
-In Texas, we are

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.332 line:0%
the last man standing.

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:21.467 line:0%
There are a lot of conservative

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.768 line:0%
and red states
around the country,

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:26.406 line:0%
but if we fall, America falls.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.873 line:0%
The electoral votes of New York,

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:29.709 line:0%
California and New York
combined together

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.944 line:0%
means we could never elect
a conservative or Republican

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:34.880 line:0%
to the White House ever again.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.083 line:0%
I can tell you

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:40.119 line:0%
that, as lieutenant governor
of this great state

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.488 line:0%
that I'm blessed
and honored to serve,

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:46.592 line:0%
[ Measuredly ]
we're not ever going
to let that happen.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:47.860
-Why do these guys
always sound like

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.029
overexcited LARPers in the park?

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.130
[ English accent ]
By order of the queen,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.000
I shall not allow this heresy.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.336
Calm down, Dan.
You work at Hobby Lobby.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.070
So now, though,
they're just admitting it.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.238
They don't want to lose Texas.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:00.506
That's what this is all about.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.875
And it's one thing to say,
"We can't lose Texas,

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.211
so we have to work on our
message and our policies."

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.380
It's another to say,
"We can't lose Texas,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.814
so we're changing the rules.

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:11.083
It's like Subway deciding
between actually using tuna

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.819
or calling it toona
and hoping no one notices.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.756
So Texas Republicans are afraid
that, if Democrats make gains,

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.391
that they could be locked
out of the White House

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.392
for the foreseeable future
and they're desperate

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:22.461
to preserve their political
power in the state

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:23.896
any way they can.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:27.066
By Patrick's own admission,
GOP success nationally depends

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.701
on Republicans keeping control
in Texas,

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.203
which is why
Texas Governor Greg Abbott

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:34.106
called a special legislative
session for this month

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:36.709
to pass a series of Draconian
voter suppression laws.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.644 line:0%
-In Texas, the state legislature

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.713 line:0%
is set to vote this week

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.815 line:0%
on two restrictive
voting bills.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:46.519 line:0%
The legislation moved forward
yesterday after a heated debate.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.721 line:0%
Critics say the measures
unfairly harm Black voters.

00:04:49.721 --> 00:04:51.324 line:0%
-The proposed Texas legislation

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:55.328 line:0%
includes banning 24-hour
and drive-through voting,

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:58.231 line:0%
new voter ID requirements
for mail-in ballots,

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:01.668 line:0%
and expanding the powers
of partisan pollwatchers.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:03.302
-They want to ban
drive-through voting?

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:05.204
How can you be
against drive-throughs?

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.074
The pandemic's been a nightmare,
but one thing it's taught me is

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:09.742
I love not having
to get out of my car.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.611
Last week I had
my appendix removed

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.646 line:0%
and I just left
the engine running.

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.081 line:0%
There's nothing --

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.882 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.017 line:0%
One more time.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.018 line:0%
What was that look?

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.053 line:0%
Great. Great.

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:22.221 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.590
Definitely glad
we saw the open cut.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.260
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.129
There's nothing more American
than a drive-through.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.830
If you ask me,
not only should you be able

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.433
to vote via drive-through,
but, while you're there,

00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.269
you should also be able
to deposit a check,

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:37.837
get your car washed,
and pick up

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.339
a Doritos Locos Taco Supreme.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.007
Doritos Locos Taco Supreme,

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:43.843
made with 100%
all-natural beeeph.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.878
That's beeeph,
with three "E's" and a "ph."

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.779
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.779 --> 00:05:49.982
These bills are obviously
designed to make voting harder

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:52.050
and, in particular,
target Black voters.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:54.487
For example, in an earlier
version of the bill,

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:55.788
it would've implemented a...

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.868
And of course they were
targeting Black voters.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.603
What other possible excuse
could they have

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.538
for banning voting
on Sunday mornings?

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.172
Did they not want to bump up

00:06:14.172 --> 00:06:16.576
against everyone's weekly
yoga in the park class?

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:18.511
Because we're all capable
of doing both.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.312
I can get up first thing
in the morning to vote

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:22.748
and then make my way over
to the top of the longmeadow

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.283
in time to do child's pose,

00:06:24.283 --> 00:06:25.484
Linda!

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:26.919
I know you're mad because I was

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.554
five minutes late last week

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.556
and I immediately skipped
to cat-cow

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.591
and you said, "You have
to start in child's pose.

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:34.026
It represents birth."
And I said,

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.562
"Oh, does it, Linda?

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.497
[ Laughter ]
Is that what it represents?

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:41.533
Can you tell me more,
since this is my first time

00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:44.403
doing yoga, Linda?"

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:45.404
[ Whispering ]
Also,

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:47.607
I know it was you
who farted, Linda.

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:48.808
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.776
[ Mouthing
"I know it was you." ]

00:06:50.776 --> 00:06:52.211
Republicans ended up
backtracking

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:54.113
and removing that provision
after a backlash,

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:57.049
although their explanation
of what happened was ludicrous.

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:59.685
They claim they weren't
targeting Black voters.

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:02.388
The bill had just been
misprinted and nobody caught it.

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:45.797
-First of all,
11:00 doesn't make

00:07:45.797 --> 00:07:46.899
any more sense than 1:00.

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:48.233
Why would banning early voting

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.669
before 11:00 am on Sunday

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:51.036
make elections more secure?

00:07:51.036 --> 00:07:53.806
You guys afraid the pollworkers
would be too hung over

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.708
to detect fraudulent ballots?

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:58.177
"Uh, my vision's super blurry
this morning,

00:07:58.177 --> 00:07:59.177
but your ID looks good to me,

00:07:59.177 --> 00:08:00.346
Mr. Cockroach."

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:03.448
"Cockroach?!
I'm a cicada, you dunderhead!"

00:08:03.448 --> 00:08:05.418
[ Laughter ]
I've never been insulted
in all my life,

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:07.787
which, as you all know,
is 17 years.

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:09.788
Seventeen years.
I'm still in my prime."

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:12.158
"Oh, you got to be 18 to vote."

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.860
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.996
"How convenient.

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:19.398
This is cicada suppression."

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:21.467
So, that provision
was eventually removed

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:24.036
after a backlash and a walkout
by Texas Democrats,

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:25.871
but, still, it's been clear
from day one

00:08:25.871 --> 00:08:27.039
what this is all about.

00:08:27.039 --> 00:08:28.140
Republicans admitted it.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.908
They want to hold on
to power in Texas.

00:08:29.908 --> 00:08:32.978
And let's also just keep in mind
that Texas is already, arguably,

00:08:32.978 --> 00:08:34.647
the most difficult state
to vote in.

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:36.449
Even just registering
to vote is a hassle.

00:08:50.896 --> 00:08:52.064
Good Lord!

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:53.165
Sounds like the directions

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:54.333
to one of those board games

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.602
you only find in upstate B&amp;Bs.

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:58.604
Anybody up for a game
of -- ooh!

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:01.874
[ Laughter ]
Oh, oh! Hold on!

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:02.874
Wi-Fi's back on.

00:09:02.874 --> 00:09:04.543
Ooh! Thank God.

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:07.913
Second, the only situation where
I'd ever want to be deputized is

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:09.315
as the nerdy sidekick

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:11.450
to an outlaw cop played
by Bruce Willis.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.751
And the whole movie,
I'd be begging him

00:09:12.751 --> 00:09:14.286
to deputize me and he'd refuse

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:15.988
and then at the end,
there'd be a climactic,

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:18.624
heartwarming moment right before
we storm the bad guys' hideout

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:20.592
where he puts his arm
on my shoulder and says...

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:21.627
[ As Willis ]
Meyers,

00:09:21.627 --> 00:09:23.896
I hereby deputize me
to be my deputy.

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:25.830
And, yes, in this movie,
I play myself,

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.433
just because it's easier.

00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:29.201
I want to have to remember
all my character details,

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:30.369
like a fake name or a job.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:31.370
I mean, despite
what you might think,

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.538
from all my flawless
impressions,

00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:34.273
I'm not a professional actor.

00:09:34.273 --> 00:09:35.440
[ Laughter ]
It's just a side hobby of mine

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.944
that I happen to be
very good at.

00:09:37.944 --> 00:09:40.246
Stanislavski begged me
to teach him.

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.181
He pleaded with me,
"Please, teach me how you do

00:09:42.181 --> 00:09:43.882
your Vince Vaughn impression."
And I'd say...

00:09:43.882 --> 00:09:45.518
[ As Vaughn ]
Buddy, buddy, buddy,
you got to relax.

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:48.186
[ Laughter ]

00:09:48.186 --> 00:09:51.123
I should admit impressions camp
was a camp you go to

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:52.591
to make you
stop doing impressions.

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:54.927
[ Laughter ]

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:57.496
-[ Clapping ]

00:09:57.496 --> 00:10:00.332
-Anyway, the rules in Texas
are already clearly skewed

00:10:00.332 --> 00:10:02.601
to the type of voters
Republicans want

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:04.337
to show up to the polls.
For example...

00:10:11.243 --> 00:10:12.745
That's really the whole game.

00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:14.079
The only way it could be
more obvious is

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:16.481
if they said you can't use
a driver's license,

00:10:16.481 --> 00:10:17.883
but you can use a...

00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:22.721
So those are the rules
that already exist in Texas.

00:10:22.721 --> 00:10:24.556
Now, Republicans want
to make it even worse,

00:10:24.556 --> 00:10:26.491
which led Texas Democrats
to flee the state,

00:10:26.491 --> 00:10:28.627
in a last-ditch attempt
to stop the bills from passing.

00:10:28.627 --> 00:10:30.563
And Fox News criticized
the Democrats

00:10:30.563 --> 00:10:32.397
for bringing beer with them.

00:10:32.397 --> 00:10:33.832 line:0%
-Texas state Democrats are

00:10:33.832 --> 00:10:36.501 line:0%
in Washington, D.C. this morning
after leaving the state

00:10:36.501 --> 00:10:38.204 line:0%
in an attempt to block
Republican efforts

00:10:38.204 --> 00:10:40.639 line:0%
to pass a bill
making it harder to vote.

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:42.775 line:0%
More than 50 House Democrats
got on a plane

00:10:42.775 --> 00:10:44.676 line:0%
and flew to D.C.
on Monday afternoon,

00:10:44.676 --> 00:10:47.513 line:0%
vowing to stay away from Texas
until next month,

00:10:47.513 --> 00:10:49.948 line:0%
so that Republicans
can't vote on anything.

00:10:49.948 --> 00:10:51.183 line:0%
Lawmakers need a quorum --

00:10:51.183 --> 00:10:52.851 line:0%
a certain number
of members present --

00:10:52.851 --> 00:10:53.952 line:0%
in order to vote.

00:10:53.952 --> 00:10:55.520 line:0%
-Fifty-eight Democrats.

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.790 line:0%
Texas Democrats,
are taking a stand

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:00.726 line:0%
against Republican
voting bills by --

00:11:00.726 --> 00:11:01.860 line:0%
What did they do?

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.163 line:0%
They hopped on a couple
of private jets

00:11:04.163 --> 00:11:05.798 line:0%
and they're flying to D.C.,
but, of course,

00:11:05.798 --> 00:11:07.366 line:0%
first, they have to take
some selfies

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:08.867 line:0%
to show the folks
what they're doing.

00:11:08.867 --> 00:11:10.469 line:0%
-And they grab the beer.

00:11:10.469 --> 00:11:13.205 line:0%
They did, a case
of Miller Lite, I think.

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:14.640
-Why do Republicans think
it's a gotcha

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.275
to point out they had a case
of Miller Lite?

00:11:16.275 --> 00:11:18.377
So what, is the GOP
really going after

00:11:18.377 --> 00:11:19.711
Texan beer drinkers now?

00:11:19.711 --> 00:11:21.146
Everyone knows real Americans

00:11:21.146 --> 00:11:23.883
drink vodka, peach Schnapps,
and cranberry juice.

00:11:23.883 --> 00:11:25.785
And, yeah,
that's a sex on the beach,

00:11:25.785 --> 00:11:26.786
or, as it's known in Texas,

00:11:26.786 --> 00:11:28.554
a throwdown at the hoedown.

00:11:28.554 --> 00:11:30.623
[ Laughter ]
Now, if you are the Republicans

00:11:30.623 --> 00:11:32.258
and you want to dispel
the impression

00:11:32.258 --> 00:11:34.726
that this is just
an authoritarian power grab,

00:11:34.726 --> 00:11:36.662
the absolute last thing
you'd want to do is threaten

00:11:36.662 --> 00:11:38.597
to arrest the Democrats
who fled the state

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:40.432
and, yet, that's exactly
what Abbott did.

00:11:40.432 --> 00:11:42.467 line:0%
-I can and I will continue

00:11:42.467 --> 00:11:44.936 line:0%
to call special session
after special session

00:11:44.936 --> 00:11:46.205 line:0%
after special session,

00:11:46.205 --> 00:11:49.375 line:0%
all the way up
until election next year.

00:11:49.375 --> 00:11:51.477 line:0%
And so if these people want
to be hanging out

00:11:51.477 --> 00:11:54.779 line:0%
wherever they're hanging out
on this taxpayer-paid junket,

00:11:54.779 --> 00:11:56.548 line:0%
they're going to have
to be prepared to do it

00:11:56.548 --> 00:11:58.050 line:0%
for well over a year.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.185 line:0%
As soon as they come back
into the state of Texas,

00:12:00.185 --> 00:12:01.353 line:0%
they will be arrested,

00:12:01.353 --> 00:12:04.056 line:0%
they will be cabined
inside the Texas Capitol,

00:12:04.056 --> 00:12:05.991 line:0%
until they get their job done.

00:12:05.991 --> 00:12:07.192
-A surefire way to make clear

00:12:07.192 --> 00:12:08.727
you're the villain
in any situation is

00:12:08.727 --> 00:12:10.195
to threaten
to arrest your opponents,

00:12:10.195 --> 00:12:11.263
especially in the South.

00:12:11.263 --> 00:12:13.065
You sound like Boss Hogg
threatening

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:14.399
to round up those Duke boys.

00:12:14.399 --> 00:12:16.168
[ As Hogg ]
Oh, I'm gonna get
them Duke boys!

00:12:16.168 --> 00:12:19.037
And, when I do, we're gonna
cabin them inside the Capitol!

00:12:19.037 --> 00:12:21.240
But, somehow, another Texas
politician managed

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.241
to outdo Abbott, in terms
of pure shamelessness

00:12:23.241 --> 00:12:26.645
and I'm sure, by now, you've
probably guessed who it was.

00:12:26.645 --> 00:12:28.847 line:0%
-What you're seeing
the Democrats do here

00:12:28.847 --> 00:12:30.516 line:0%
is a political stunt.

00:12:30.516 --> 00:12:31.884 line:0%
And, you know,
I will say it's ironic

00:12:31.884 --> 00:12:33.652 line:0%
because they were getting
on their private jet

00:12:33.652 --> 00:12:35.654 line:0%
to fly to Washington, D.C.

00:12:35.654 --> 00:12:37.856 line:0%
They almost surely had
to show identification

00:12:37.856 --> 00:12:39.357 line:0%
to get on that jet.
-[ Laughs ]

00:12:39.357 --> 00:12:41.693 line:0%
-And, yet, they're doing
this in a fit

00:12:41.693 --> 00:12:45.063 line:0%
because they don't want
mail-in ballots to be verified.

00:12:45.063 --> 00:12:46.932 line:0%
They don't want the signatures
to be verified.

00:12:46.932 --> 00:12:49.901 line:0%
They don't want
basic integrity steps

00:12:49.901 --> 00:12:52.538 line:0%
to be strengthened
in the state of Texas.

00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:54.373 line:0%
This is, at the end
of the day, politics,

00:12:54.373 --> 00:12:56.508 line:0%
and they need to get back
to doing their jobs.

00:12:56.508 --> 00:12:59.478
-It's not ironic that they had
to show ID to get on a plane,

00:12:59.478 --> 00:13:01.646
since, unlike voting,
flying on a plane

00:13:01.646 --> 00:13:04.016
is not a sacred right protected
by the Constitution.

00:13:04.016 --> 00:13:06.317
There's no Article 10
that grants every American

00:13:06.317 --> 00:13:08.720
the right to get your elbow
slammed by a drink cart

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.723
while the dude across from you
spends 10 minutes trying

00:13:10.723 --> 00:13:11.891
to cram a suitcase

00:13:11.891 --> 00:13:13.492
into an overhead compartment
that's too small.

00:13:13.492 --> 00:13:15.027
Of course,
if Republicans really wanted

00:13:15.027 --> 00:13:17.062
to treat flying
the way they treat voting,

00:13:17.062 --> 00:13:18.597
then every plane
would be forced to idle

00:13:18.597 --> 00:13:20.866
on the tarmac for hours,
while they wait to take off

00:13:20.866 --> 00:13:22.802
because there's only
one runway open

00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:24.402
and it would be illegal
to serve snacks,

00:13:24.402 --> 00:13:26.872
not even SunChips,
which are barely food.

00:13:26.872 --> 00:13:29.507
It's like eating
salsa-flavored packing peanuts.

00:13:29.507 --> 00:13:31.643
I'm pretty sure there's less
actual food in SunChips

00:13:31.643 --> 00:13:33.278
than there are in Subway tuna.

00:13:33.278 --> 00:13:34.413 line:0%
Republicans have come out
and said

00:13:34.413 --> 00:13:35.747 line:0%
what this is really all about --

00:13:35.747 --> 00:13:37.316 line:0%
they don't want to lose Texas
and they're willing

00:13:37.316 --> 00:13:39.351 line:0%
to change the rules
to stop that from happening.

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:41.353
It couldn't be more obvious.
They admitted it.

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:42.721
They just haven't
succeeded yet.

00:13:42.721 --> 00:13:44.522
They couldn't pass
these bills the first time.

00:13:44.522 --> 00:13:46.258
They might not be able
to pass them this time,

00:13:46.258 --> 00:13:47.993
so if they want
to ram them through,

00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:49.594
they're going to have to try
at least...

00:13:49.594 --> 00:13:50.796
-Three times!

00:13:50.796 --> 00:13:53.665
[ Horns blaring ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

